# Forge local end-user testing — template only. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
# IMPORTANT: nothing in this repository loads `.env` automatically. There is no
# dotenv dependency in the Rust host, the Tauri CLI, or Vite. The native host
# reads these from its own process environment, so a `.env` file takes effect
# only if you load it into the shell that launches Forge. See
# `infra/local/README.md` for the exact command.
#
# `.env` is gitignored; this `.env.example` is deliberately not. Never commit a
# filled-in copy, and never paste a real key into any tracked file.

# Required for the OpenAI direct-provider path.
# Create one at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys. The key needs access to
# the Responses API and to whichever model you select in the app
# (default: gpt-5-mini).
OPENAI_API_KEY=replace-me

# Optional, and rarely useful. The host validates this and accepts ONLY
# https://api.openai.com/v1 — any other host, scheme, port, or path is
# rejected at startup. A local proxy, gateway, or self-hosted model endpoint
# will NOT work here. Leave unset unless you have a specific reason.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
